    "rich_text_intro": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Garlic, dill, chili flakes and a pinch of turmeric for colour, left on the fish long enough to actually get in &mdash; then baked and broken into big, forkable flakes rather than plated as a tidy fillet. It is a platter dish, not a portion dish, and it is better for it.</p><p>Two things make it work. The salt goes on at the oven rather than in the bowl, which keeps the texture soft instead of firm. And the dill goes in twice &mdash; once into the marinade where it turns grassy and soft, once over the top at the table where it stays sharp.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
